    "body": "Findings (agent, M5) - `stock_engine_agreement --ignored`, release, run in full at each commit:\n\n| tree | FINDINGs | result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `3713901d^1` (main just before PR #414) | 0 | 3 passed |\n| `3713901d` (merge of PR #414, #402 true arcs in the **column** engine) | 6465 | 2 failed |\n| `5fd2b93a` (main at filing) | 6465 | 2 failed |\n| `be650bb3` (PR #483 head, #413 true arcs in the **field** engine) | **0** | **3 passed** (107 s) |\n\n**One cause.** The lane went red at the PR #414 merge (`3713901d`). That merge moved the column engine onto the true XY circle, but the field engine still cut the inscribed chords. All 6465 findings are in programs with `Arc` records (finish3d_waterline_cone 4980, project_dome 616, contour_plate_with_hole+bull 351, radial_dome 321, face_square_blended 46, tangential_lead 37, plate_with_hole 29, disc_hole 29, and the four plateau programs plus scallop+bull at 9-12 each). The arc-free `slot_wide_channel_rows` was clean throughout. The field engine was the wrong one: chords inside the arc. PR #483 fixes it, and no disagreement is left, so no tolerance needs justifying.\n\nNo code change is needed beyond #483, so no separate PR. This issue is done when #483 merges (#483 says `Fixes #413` only, so close this one by hand then and name the #483 merge commit).\n",
